WEBVTT

00:35.425 --> 00:38.595
You guys are gonna love this spa.
They give the best massages.

00:38.762 --> 00:40.596
Your whole bodies
will feel like Joe's legs.

00:40.763 --> 00:43.766
- Wow.
- That would be nice for a short period.

00:43.933 --> 00:46.935
I tell you, I need this.
I've had a really stressful morning.

00:47.102 --> 00:51.356
Wait a minute.
Doc, are you telling me that it's 8:25?

00:51.523 --> 00:53.273
<i>Precisely.
- Damn.</i>

00:53.440 --> 00:55.317
I'm late for school.

01:14.918 --> 01:17.964
Okay, why don't you just
get yourself settled up on the table.

01:18.130 --> 01:21.424
- I'll give you a minute.
- Uh, what am I supposed...?

01:28.097 --> 01:30.891
- You ready in there?
Yup.

01:31.267 --> 01:34.311
Oh, ha, ha.
You put some fake poo on the floor.

01:34.478 --> 01:35.604
Oh, no.

01:35.771 --> 01:38.815
Get out. Get out. Scat.

01:39.148 --> 01:42.026
Ah. This is more like it.

01:49.449 --> 01:50.743
- Is the music okay?
- Actually...

01:50.910 --> 01:53.662
...would you mind tuning it to 97. 1?

01:53.829 --> 01:55.998
<i>You're listening to The Quiet Storm.</i>

01:56.164 --> 01:58.583
<i>Up next, the music of The Isleys...</i>

01:58.749 --> 02:01.335
<i>...Teddy Pendergrass, and right now,
here's some Marvin Gaye.</i>

02:03.337 --> 02:05.923
Oh, that's what I'm talking about.

02:06.382 --> 02:09.343
Oh, this is long overdue.

02:09.510 --> 02:12.261
There's nothing
like a good suit massage.

02:12.428 --> 02:17.057
Focus on the lapels.
That's where I carry most of my stress.

02:17.348 --> 02:20.518
Okay, here's one. If you were gay
and you had to have sex...

02:20.685 --> 02:23.980
...with either John Forsythe
or Sean Connery, who would it be?

02:24.147 --> 02:25.898
Oh, that's easy. John Forsythe.

02:26.065 --> 02:28.401
- Yeah, John Forsythe.
- John Forsythe, absolutely.

02:28.568 --> 02:31.403
It's funny, I'd also say John Forsythe.
I was just curious.

02:31.570 --> 02:34.489
Yeah,
I mean, Sean Connery is just so...

02:34.656 --> 02:35.699
Uh-oh.

02:35.866 --> 02:37.992
Oh, God. I am so sorry.

02:38.159 --> 02:40.954
It's too late. The damage is done.

02:44.498 --> 02:48.085
<i>Hey, Chris, you know what I just got?
The boxed set of Lord of the Rings.</i>

02:48.252 --> 02:49.754
- It's awesome.
- Yeah.

02:49.919 --> 02:52.505
Remember the giant eagle
they rode in the first one...

02:52.672 --> 02:54.716
...that then rescues them
at the third one?

02:54.884 --> 02:55.926
- Yeah, yeah.
- Yeah.

02:56.093 --> 02:58.094
Why didn't they fly the eagle
to Mordor...

02:58.261 --> 03:00.847
...instead of spending three movies
walking there?

03:01.014 --> 03:03.682
That's not what it's about, Chris.
It's about the quest.

03:03.849 --> 03:06.518
I'm not arguing.
I'm saying there's a hole in the story.

03:06.685 --> 03:08.979
- Did you like the movie?
- That's not the point.

03:09.146 --> 03:11.815
- Did you like the movie?
- Of course, I loved the movie.

03:11.982 --> 03:13.108
But look I'm no writer.

03:13.275 --> 03:16.819
But if a fat kid like me with one finger
up his nose is bumped by it...

03:16.986 --> 03:18.654
...someone would have caught it.

03:18.821 --> 03:20.281
So you didn't like the eagle?

03:20.448 --> 03:23.241
Well, no, I did,
the eagle was majestic and beautiful...

03:23.408 --> 03:27.830
...but sometimes you have to sacrifice
spectacle for a coherent storyline.

03:27.997 --> 03:29.164
Oh.

03:29.331 --> 03:31.500
<i>- Have you ever seen Krull?
- No.</i>

03:31.666 --> 03:33.627
<i>Yeah, you don't need to see Krull.</i>

03:33.794 --> 03:36.628
The best thing you can do
for your body after a massage...

03:36.795 --> 03:39.005
...is hot coffee, alcohol
and Slim Jims.

03:39.172 --> 03:41.091
Oh, Dad, I'm glad you're here.

03:41.257 --> 03:43.217
There's something I need to ask you.

03:43.383 --> 03:45.053
- What is it, Chris?
- Well, um...

03:45.220 --> 03:48.639
...today in gym class,
I noticed one of my testicles...

03:48.806 --> 03:52.267
...went up inside my body,
and it hasn't come back out yet.

03:52.434 --> 03:54.019
And I'm a little scared.

03:54.186 --> 03:57.063
Sir, this employee
just made a sexual remark to me.

03:57.230 --> 03:59.273
No, Dad, I'm really worried.

03:59.440 --> 04:01.235
See, look. Is that normal?

04:01.401 --> 04:05.029
Ah, ah. Sir. Sir, your employee
is exposing himself to me.

04:05.196 --> 04:07.490
- But, Dad.
- You got a lawsuit on your hands.

04:07.657 --> 04:09.074
Okay, look, look.

04:09.241 --> 04:13.411
If you'd be willing to forget
this happened, I'll give you this gas card.

04:13.578 --> 04:17.707
Unlimited free gas for a year.
Just because I threatened to sue you?

04:17.874 --> 04:21.293
That, and you're not the worst-looking
guy who's ever come in here.

04:21.460 --> 04:23.838
That's what I wanted to hear.

04:27.966 --> 04:31.719
Wow, Peter. A free gas card.
This could save us a lot of money.

04:31.886 --> 04:34.472
Yeah, everyone except Brian
because he bought a Prius.

04:34.639 --> 04:35.682
What a dumb-ass.

04:37.392 --> 04:39.352
What? What did I miss?
Are we laughing at Brian?

04:39.519 --> 04:41.812
Ah, Brian, you suck.

04:41.979 --> 04:43.772
What the devil is in here?

04:43.939 --> 04:47.234
I threw out all your apple juice, Stewie.
We're a gas family now.

04:47.400 --> 04:49.570
You put gasoline in Stewie's bottle?

04:49.736 --> 04:52.739
You damn fool!
You're more useless than Aquaman.

04:54.657 --> 04:57.034
Help! Somebody help! Rape!

04:57.201 --> 04:59.661
Scream all you want.
Nobody can hear you out here.

04:59.828 --> 05:01.036
I can.

05:01.203 --> 05:02.454
Aquaman, help!

05:02.621 --> 05:04.915
Hey. Hey. Hey, let her go.

05:05.082 --> 05:06.126
Or what?

05:06.293 --> 05:07.668
Or... Or...

05:07.835 --> 05:09.461
I don't know, man, but you're...

05:09.628 --> 05:12.548
You're lucky you're not doing that
over here in the ocean...

05:12.715 --> 05:15.049
...or else... Or I would stop you.

05:15.216 --> 05:16.718
For God's sakes, help!

05:16.884 --> 05:19.220
Do something!

05:19.387 --> 05:22.890
If you don't like starfish, you're
gonna be mad about what I just did.

05:23.057 --> 05:24.767
Oh, God! Help!

05:24.934 --> 05:28.895
Oh, you're in for it now, buddy.
I got, like, five fish coming to help.

05:29.062 --> 05:30.689
Oh, oh, here they are.

05:30.856 --> 05:32.774
Help! He's hurting me!

05:32.941 --> 05:34.692
Maybe you shouldn't have led him on.

05:39.239 --> 05:40.948
Peter, what the hell is that?

05:41.115 --> 05:42.825
It's a space shuttle, Lois.

05:42.992 --> 05:46.494
I figured with unlimited free gas,
I could afford to go into space.

05:46.661 --> 05:48.622
Why is it every time I open this door...

05:48.788 --> 05:52.083
...you seem to be in some vehicle
you've inexplicably acquired?

05:52.250 --> 05:54.418
I got this at a NASA auction
for next to nothing.

05:54.586 --> 05:57.088
They were gonna scrap it
because there's some problem.

05:57.255 --> 05:59.423
Instead they sold it to me.
Simple explanation.

05:59.590 --> 06:03.344
I do not want you trying to fly that.
You're not even a trained astronaut.

06:03.510 --> 06:06.429
Relax, Lois, nothing bad ever happens
to space shuttles.

06:06.596 --> 06:08.514
Now, stand back.

06:20.442 --> 06:22.319
I'm back from space, everybody.

06:22.486 --> 06:23.861
You got lucky, Peter.

06:24.028 --> 06:26.363
- How was it, Dad?
- Oh, mind-boggling, Chris.

06:26.529 --> 06:29.033
Barreling around the earth
at five miles per second.

06:29.200 --> 06:32.827
Watching the sun rise
over the Sea of Japan, it's indescribable.

06:32.994 --> 06:35.955
I had lots of time to masturbate,
which in space, is great.

06:36.122 --> 06:38.457
Except,
it's like living in a snow globe.

06:38.624 --> 06:42.044
Peter, instead of wasting your gas
on a series of comedic stunts...

06:42.211 --> 06:44.381
...why don't you use it
more constructively?

06:44.547 --> 06:46.465
I mean,
we could take a family vacation.

06:46.632 --> 06:48.133
Yeah, that's a great idea, Mom.

06:48.300 --> 06:50.260
<i>Maybe we can go to the island
from Lost.</i>

06:50.427 --> 06:53.346
No, I don't want to listen
to Matthew Fox's heavy breathing.

06:54.806 --> 06:57.683
Kate, you don't get it.

06:57.849 --> 07:00.144
We are the island.

07:02.522 --> 07:04.815
Hand me that paper bag.

07:06.525 --> 07:08.693
Jack, that's got my poop in it.

07:08.860 --> 07:09.986
I know.

07:10.153 --> 07:11.278
I know.

07:11.445 --> 07:13.280
It's got a hint of coconut in it.

07:13.447 --> 07:15.032
And something else.

07:15.199 --> 07:17.576
But that's part of the mystery.

07:22.498 --> 07:24.582
Everybody up,
we're going on vacation.

07:24.749 --> 07:27.460
Car leaves at 6 a. m. Sharp.

07:31.755 --> 07:33.216
Oh, fuck!

07:33.383 --> 07:36.344
You blow that fucking horn again,
I swear to God...

07:36.511 --> 07:39.721
...I will ram that fucking thing
up your goddamn ass!

07:40.472 --> 07:43.392
All aboard for the Grand Canyon.

07:47.727 --> 07:49.397
Oh, I know you're tired, Stewie...

07:49.564 --> 07:51.982
...but you can sleep all you want
in the car.

07:52.148 --> 07:53.859
Oh, 6 a. m.

07:54.025 --> 07:57.278
I shouldn't have stayed up all night
listening to Persian radio.

07:57.444 --> 08:00.239
<i>Hey, that was
Roxette with "You've Got the Look. "</i>

08:00.406 --> 08:04.409
<i>It's 21:00
and still 27 centigrade out there.</i>

08:04.576 --> 08:05.786
<i>Oh, that's hot.</i>

08:05.953 --> 08:08.539
<i>If you're cruising
along the left side of the road...</i>

08:08.706 --> 08:11.958
<i>...at 120 kilometers per hour
in the Shahabi Desert...</i>

08:12.125 --> 08:13.376
<i>...turn up the decibels...</i>

08:13.543 --> 08:19.798
<i>...because it's Shaleb Mami
with Zahec Malec on 103.2, the Hoch.</i>

08:21.091 --> 08:22.594
What's with all those birds?

08:22.759 --> 08:24.094
My tropical bird collection.

08:24.261 --> 08:26.096
- Just in case.
- Just in case, what?

08:26.263 --> 08:28.307
We're not gonna need
a dozen tropical birds.

08:28.473 --> 08:31.142
Oh, I was not aware
that you could see the future, Lois.

08:31.309 --> 08:33.644
Can I go ahead
and get tomorrow's lottery number?

08:33.811 --> 08:34.854
Stupid woman.

08:35.021 --> 08:37.439
Peter, you are not putting those birds
in the car.

08:37.606 --> 08:40.276
Oh, well, then I guess
we're not going on vacation.

08:40.860 --> 08:43.069
Good, then I'm going back to bed.

08:43.987 --> 08:46.531
All right, Peter,
you can bring the stupid birds.

08:46.698 --> 08:49.992
Yay. You're letting me be myself.
All right, everybody, lets go.

08:52.077 --> 08:55.123
All right, everybody, off we go.
We are gonna have such a great time...

08:56.498 --> 08:58.000
<i>- Hello.
Hey, Peter. What's up?</i>

08:58.167 --> 09:00.586
Hey, Quagmire.
Just taking the family on vacation.

09:00.753 --> 09:04.339
<i>That's good. Hang on. I'm stuck behind
some fat ass driving too slow.</i>

09:04.505 --> 09:05.548
<i>Come on, stupid. Move it.</i>

09:06.924 --> 09:09.426
Hang on, Quagmire.
Some jerk behind me is honking his horn.

09:09.593 --> 09:11.095
<i>Oh, you should flip him off.</i>

09:11.261 --> 09:13.055
<i>Hang on. Some fat ass flipped me off.</i>

09:13.221 --> 09:14.723
<i>Hey, up yours, you jerk.</i>

09:14.890 --> 09:16.849
Hang on, I gotta kick this guy's ass.

09:17.016 --> 09:18.601
<i>Yeah, I gotta kick this guy's ass.</i>

09:18.768 --> 09:20.644
<i>I'll call you after the fight.
Me too.</i>

09:20.811 --> 09:23.438
<i>Good luck in yours.
Good luck in yours.</i>

09:34.531 --> 09:37.117
Lois. I'm awake, Lois.

09:37.284 --> 09:38.369
Lois!

09:39.078 --> 09:40.245
Lois?

09:40.412 --> 09:41.996
Where the devil is everyone?

09:42.163 --> 09:45.542
This place is more deserted
than James Gandolfini's workout room.

09:54.674 --> 09:57.594
Just waiting for my breakfast.

09:57.761 --> 09:59.179
Lois!

09:59.346 --> 10:01.473
I know how to get her attention.

10:02.432 --> 10:05.477
Lois, I'm about to drink my first soda.

10:05.644 --> 10:07.728
Better come stop me.

10:07.895 --> 10:09.688
Mmm. That must be the sugar.

10:09.855 --> 10:12.441
Oh, God, that's good.

10:13.192 --> 10:15.652
Rupert, suddenly I want to run.
Chase me.

10:24.619 --> 10:26.329
Oh, now I'm sad.

10:29.414 --> 10:31.375
Brian, do me a favor
and check on Stewie.

10:31.542 --> 10:32.961
- Would you?
- He's fine.

10:33.128 --> 10:35.420
Hey, what do you say
we sing a driving song?

12:13.341 --> 12:14.842
That was good. That was good.

12:15.009 --> 12:17.886
Chris, you were a little early
at the start of bar four.

12:18.053 --> 12:21.389
- How did that sound from your end?
- Sounded great. You want another?

12:21.556 --> 12:23.975
- Lf that works, we're fine.
- All good on my end.

12:24.142 --> 12:25.392
All right. That's a take.

12:28.146 --> 12:29.773
There's no sign of them anywhere.

12:29.939 --> 12:31.023
Meg.

12:31.190 --> 12:33.359
Chris. Brian.

12:33.776 --> 12:34.902
They're gone.

12:35.069 --> 12:36.528
I'm all alone.

12:36.695 --> 12:38.655
I can do whatever I want.

12:38.821 --> 12:40.823
Heh, heh, I'm gonna take
Brian's novel...

12:40.990 --> 12:44.994
...and replace every use
of the word "and" with the word "fart. "

12:45.453 --> 12:48.331
"The young soldier fart his brother
looked at each other.

12:48.498 --> 12:52.209
Fart both knew
that with love fart truth fart courage...

12:52.376 --> 12:55.170
...they would both emerge
st-farting on their feet. "

12:55.337 --> 12:57.046
That one didn't work.

12:58.756 --> 13:02.844
Let's see what fascinating pubescent
treasures Chris has got hidden away.

13:03.011 --> 13:05.012
<i>Ooh, Hustler magazine.</i>

13:05.179 --> 13:07.473
I finally get to see
what a vagina looks...

13:07.640 --> 13:10.517
Oh, God. Oh, my God. Oh, my God.

13:14.396 --> 13:16.273
You can't hurt...

13:16.440 --> 13:19.692
...anyone anymore.

13:25.071 --> 13:28.157
Why New York? I thought we were going
to the Grand Canyon.

13:28.324 --> 13:31.409
Well, I just thought we should stop
and pay our respects.

13:33.287 --> 13:34.747
Ground Zero.

13:34.914 --> 13:37.332
So this is where the first guy
got AIDS.

13:37.499 --> 13:40.460
Peter, this is the site
of the 9/11 terrorist attacks.

13:40.627 --> 13:42.753
- Oh, so Saddam Hussein did this?
- No.

13:42.920 --> 13:44.046
- The Iraqi Army?
- No.

13:44.213 --> 13:45.422
- Some guys from Iraq?
- No.

13:45.589 --> 13:47.383
That lady who visited Iraq one time?

13:47.550 --> 13:49.260
Iraq had nothing to do with this.

13:49.426 --> 13:51.804
It was Saudi Arabians,
Lebanese and Egyptians...

13:51.971 --> 13:54.473
...financed by a Saudi Arabian guy
in Afghanistan...

13:54.640 --> 13:56.349
...and sheltered by Pakistanis.

13:56.516 --> 13:59.185
So you're saying
we need to invade Iran?

14:01.771 --> 14:03.438
Wake up, Stewie.

14:03.605 --> 14:06.693
Let's get you out of that seat
and into a fresh diaper.

14:06.860 --> 14:07.944
Oh, my God.

14:08.111 --> 14:10.154
Peter, Stewie's not in the car.

14:10.320 --> 14:12.197
Oh, my God,
We must've left him at home.

14:12.364 --> 14:16.492
Oh, my God. That is hilarious.

14:16.659 --> 14:18.327
He is probably freaking out.

14:18.494 --> 14:20.998
God, I would give anything
to see his face right now.

14:21.165 --> 14:22.206
He's probably all like...

14:22.373 --> 14:24.500
Where...? Where the deuce is everyone?

14:24.667 --> 14:26.544
I can't really do a good Stewie.

14:26.711 --> 14:28.920
Oh, my God.
What kind of a mother am I?

14:29.087 --> 14:30.839
Peter, we gotta go home right now.

14:31.006 --> 14:34.342
Great, Lois, now we gotta bail
on the whole vacation. This sucks.

14:34.509 --> 14:36.552
Now every time
I come back to this place...

14:36.719 --> 14:39.681
...it's gonna be associated
with one particular bad memory.

14:39.848 --> 14:43.225
We could call Quagmire and Cleveland.
They can go and check on Stewie.

14:43.392 --> 14:45.686
They'd look after him
till we got home.

14:45.853 --> 14:48.478
Well, okay, I guess so.

14:48.645 --> 14:50.689
Quagmire and Cleveland
are great with kids.

14:50.856 --> 14:52.816
<i>Like Robin Williams in Patch Adams.</i>

14:52.983 --> 14:56.320
Huh. Everybody's lying around in here.
Liar, liar, pants on fire.

14:56.486 --> 14:59.656
What am I, in Congress? Ha-ha.
See, laughter is the best medicine.

14:59.823 --> 15:02.742
Please, sir, I'm in so much pain.

15:02.909 --> 15:05.286
Shut up and listen to my material.
Huh, what's this?

15:05.453 --> 15:07.537
Bedpan. Peter Pan.
Next stop is Neverland.

15:07.704 --> 15:10.207
Come, Wendy, fly with me. Ha-ha.

15:14.753 --> 15:17.631
Hmm. I've never executed
a diaper change before.

15:17.797 --> 15:20.507
How hard can it be?
You just unfasten these things.

15:20.674 --> 15:24.595
Then lay back with your legs in the air
and let nature do the rest.

15:25.763 --> 15:27.389
Hmm. It's still there.

15:27.556 --> 15:30.267
Usually, the doody has disappeared
by now, but it hasn't.

15:30.434 --> 15:33.228
It's just sitting there
like Joseph on his wedding night.

15:35.521 --> 15:38.274
Happiest night of my life, honey.

15:39.025 --> 15:41.401
Really memorable.

15:42.194 --> 15:44.864
- Almost done in there, God?
Shut up.

15:46.324 --> 15:47.449
Intruders.

15:47.616 --> 15:50.202
Stewie, you in there?

15:53.412 --> 15:55.206
You think he's here?

15:57.792 --> 15:59.835
Oh, God. It's Cleveland and Bob Hope.

16:00.002 --> 16:02.463
The damage is done.
Better get them out of here.

16:02.630 --> 16:04.382
I'll shackle them in the basement...

16:04.548 --> 16:08.009
...with a 24-hour broadcast
of the DirecTV Help channel.

16:09.177 --> 16:11.221
What the hell? Where are we?

16:11.388 --> 16:14.222
<i>Getting to know your
remote is easier than you might think.</i>

16:14.389 --> 16:17.184
<i>These buttons at the top
control volume, channel...</i>

16:17.351 --> 16:19.019
<i>...and the power on your receiver.</i>

16:19.186 --> 16:21.270
<i>To see what else is playing,
press "guide"...</i>

16:21.437 --> 16:24.440
<i>...and scroll through the menu
by pushing the arrow button.</i>

16:24.607 --> 16:28.318
<i>Or to scroll even faster use
the channel up or channel down button.</i>

16:28.485 --> 16:32.156
<i>Now you're on your way to experiencing
all that Direc TV has to offer.</i>

16:32.322 --> 16:34.991
<i>- Now we've learned the basics...
- This may be messed up.</i>

16:35.158 --> 16:37.494
But am I the only one
getting a boner right now?

16:37.661 --> 16:40.579
Is there anything
that doesn't give you a boner, Glenn?

16:40.746 --> 16:43.082
People who use "rubbish"
when they mean garbage.

16:43.249 --> 16:45.334
- Really?
- Yup, not even a wiggle down there.

16:45.500 --> 16:47.502
<i>Your shows will appear on my playlist.</i>

16:48.087 --> 16:49.588
Peter, it's been eight hours...

16:49.755 --> 16:52.382
...and I haven't heard back
from Cleveland or Quagmire.

16:52.549 --> 16:53.925
I even tried Joe.

16:54.092 --> 16:55.218
This is my wheelchair.

16:55.385 --> 16:57.720
There are many like it.
But this one is mine.

16:57.887 --> 16:59.888
Without me, my wheelchair is useless.

17:00.055 --> 17:01.765
Without my wheelchair, I am useless.

17:03.142 --> 17:04.769
- Shut up.
- Okay.

17:07.646 --> 17:10.440
Oh, this sucks.
I wanna see the Grand Canyon.

17:10.607 --> 17:13.192
I'm sorry, but we are not leaving Stewie
by himself.

17:13.359 --> 17:14.485
We're going home.

17:17.655 --> 17:20.490
No way,
those guys have a TV in their car.

17:20.658 --> 17:23.161
<i>Heh, heh. They're watching
Operation: Dumbo Screw...</i>

17:23.327 --> 17:24.495
...with Don Knotts.

17:24.661 --> 17:26.746
<i>You've got
to impregnate this elephant...</i>

17:26.913 --> 17:29.082
<i>...or the entire species
will become extinct.</i>

17:29.249 --> 17:32.209
<i>You mean I gotta put this thing
in that thing?</i>

17:32.376 --> 17:35.504
<i>Well, this is a job
that's not worth the money.</i>

17:35.671 --> 17:37.089
Peter, watch the road.

17:37.256 --> 17:39.632
Lois, get off my back.
I'm trying to watch TV.

17:39.799 --> 17:42.760
I swear to God, I think your head's
screwed on backwards.

17:42.927 --> 17:45.012
I mean, do you have any idea...

17:54.187 --> 17:57.523
Hey, crashie,
what are you doing down there?

18:02.862 --> 18:06.656
Well, Rupert, we're out of food, diapers,
and just about everything else.

18:06.823 --> 18:08.617
Which means I've got to get a job.

18:08.783 --> 18:11.995
Otherwise, we'll be in worse shape
than Morbidly Obese Albert.

18:12.162 --> 18:14.915
Morbidly Obese Albert,
we brought you some chocolates.

18:15.081 --> 18:19.126
Oh, I can't eat those chocolates
on account of my diabetes.

18:19.293 --> 18:21.503
Remember, they had to take my foot?

18:21.670 --> 18:23.047
Look on the bright side.

18:23.213 --> 18:24.797
Now you get your shoes half price.

18:24.964 --> 18:26.383
Ha, ha, ha.

18:26.550 --> 18:29.553
All right, maybe I'll have one.

18:33.473 --> 18:35.725
Welcome to McBurgertown.
Can I take your order?

18:35.892 --> 18:37.559
You've gotta clean the bathroom.

18:37.726 --> 18:39.478
No, no. I'm not going back in there.

18:39.645 --> 18:42.523
I'm not giving you a choice.
You've gotta go clean that up.

18:42.690 --> 18:45.400
No. No.
It was literally only on the floor.

18:45.567 --> 18:47.653
There was no attempt
to get near the toilet.

18:47.819 --> 18:50.696
It's like they just pressed their buttocks
against the wall.

18:50.863 --> 18:53.240
The only part of the floor
that didn't have poo...

18:53.407 --> 18:55.534
...was the part that had a baby on it.
- Go!

18:58.913 --> 19:01.998
- Peter, did you get the train tickets?
- Actually, no, Lois.

19:02.165 --> 19:05.459
There was a guy selling shower curtain
rings. So I bought a bunch.

19:05.626 --> 19:07.795
Peter, that was the last of our cash.

19:07.961 --> 19:10.129
These ones have helium
so they are very light.

19:10.296 --> 19:11.464
You are unbelievable.

19:11.631 --> 19:13.675
The last 4 days
have been a living hell.

19:13.841 --> 19:15.551
Our baby is at home all by himself.

19:15.718 --> 19:19.597
Yet instead of getting us home,
you've managed to make things worse.

19:19.764 --> 19:22.224
A monkey
would be a refreshing step up from you.

19:22.391 --> 19:24.184
A monkey would talk less.

19:25.352 --> 19:28.604
Here's a tip. If your instinct
tells you to do something, don't!

19:28.771 --> 19:31.107
If your instinct tells you
not to do something...

19:31.274 --> 19:33.443
...it's probably the right thing to do.

19:34.569 --> 19:36.278
You wanna hurt me?

19:36.445 --> 19:38.447
Go ahead,
if it makes you feel any better.

19:38.614 --> 19:39.907
I'm an easy target.

19:40.074 --> 19:41.534
Yeah, you're right.

19:41.699 --> 19:43.618
I talk too much.

19:43.785 --> 19:46.037
I also listen too much.

19:46.204 --> 19:48.957
I could be a cold-hearted cynic
like you.

19:49.124 --> 19:51.668
But I don't like
to hurt people's feelings.

19:51.835 --> 19:54.837
Well, you think what you want
about me. I'm not changing.

19:55.003 --> 19:57.047
I like... I like me.

19:57.214 --> 19:58.924
My kids like me.

19:59.091 --> 20:01.259
My friends like me.

20:01.426 --> 20:03.010
Because I'm the real article.

20:03.177 --> 20:05.431
What you see is what you get.

20:09.892 --> 20:12.353
Ha, ha, ha. Movie references.

20:12.520 --> 20:15.605
Guys, I found us a ride to Quahog
in the back of a truck. Hurry!

20:15.772 --> 20:16.940
Oh, thank God.

20:17.107 --> 20:18.942
Let's head home before
Stewie gets hurt.

20:19.109 --> 20:21.278
Like Fozzie Bear
when he went to Saudi Arabia.

20:21.444 --> 20:23.155
It's good to worship Allah...

20:23.321 --> 20:26.282
...because I used to worship some-ah!
Wokka, wokka.

20:28.116 --> 20:30.827
I once knew a guy who was so Arab...

20:30.994 --> 20:32.453
How Arab was he?

20:32.620 --> 20:35.789
Uh, he was so Arab
that everybody liked him...

20:35.956 --> 20:38.251
...and there was nothing funny
about him at all.

20:43.046 --> 20:45.090
Can I see you in my office
for a second?

20:45.257 --> 20:49.343
- Yeah. What's up, Eric, everything okay?
- Yeah, just come into my office.

20:50.678 --> 20:53.348
Stewie, Shawanda said
she saw you sneaking food.

20:53.514 --> 20:55.141
What?

20:55.308 --> 20:58.227
She said she saw you in the kitchen
sneaking a fish sandwich.

20:58.394 --> 21:00.645
Oh, come on, dude.

21:00.812 --> 21:01.855
Yes, okay.

21:02.022 --> 21:04.649
But the thing was five minutes
past the throw-out time.

21:04.816 --> 21:08.277
Well, be that as it may, Shawanda
took these pictures on her cell phone.

21:13.866 --> 21:15.034
You're fired.

21:18.370 --> 21:19.662
We're broke, Rupert.

21:19.829 --> 21:21.873
I'm jobless. There's no food left.

21:22.040 --> 21:25.168
I'm out of diapers.
And I'm down to Meg's last hat.

21:25.335 --> 21:26.878
We're doomed, you know.

21:27.045 --> 21:30.548
Let it be written on my tombstone
that my life was considerably better...

21:30.715 --> 21:32.133
...with my family around.

21:32.300 --> 21:35.385
And I didn't realize it
until it was too late.

21:44.227 --> 21:45.770
Mommy. Daddy.

21:45.937 --> 21:48.272
Chris. Dog. Brian.

21:48.439 --> 21:49.482
They're home.

21:53.067 --> 21:55.778
Oh, Mommy, thank God, you're home.

21:55.945 --> 21:57.863
Oh, Stewie, my baby.

21:58.030 --> 22:00.908
I promise with all my heart
that I'll never say or do...

22:01.075 --> 22:03.702
...anything bad to you
for the rest of the evening.

22:03.869 --> 22:08.122
By the way, I disabled the V-chip,
and I watched so much porn.

22:08.289 --> 22:11.376
Oh, sweetie,
I'm so glad you're all right.

22:11.542 --> 22:13.460
No thanks to Cleveland and Quagmire.

22:13.627 --> 22:15.046
Wonder what happened to them?

22:15.213 --> 22:17.173
You're ready to enjoy the full range...

22:17.340 --> 22:19.758
...of exciting
DirecTV programming options.

22:19.925 --> 22:22.302
For answers to any questions
you may have...

22:22.469 --> 22:24.596
...you can consult
the onscreen help menu...

22:24.763 --> 22:31.811
...or 24-hour online assistance
is available at www. DirecTV.com/help.

22:31.977 --> 22:34.438
So sit back and enjoy DirecTV.

22:34.605 --> 22:36.482
Thanks for joining us.

22:36.649 --> 22:38.942
Welcome
to the DirecTV Help Channel.

22:39.109 --> 22:42.862
Your destination for getting started
with your new DirecTV system.

22:43.029 --> 22:44.072
Fuck! Fuck! Fuck!

22:44.239 --> 22:45.656
Fuck! Fuck!

22:45.657 --> 23:46.657
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru